crime-assist-mainmenu = Welcome to Crime Assist. Articles follow Space Law (PK). Same _XX categories do not stack — charge the heaviest. Over 35 minutes, permabrig is recommended.
crime-assist-question-isitterrorism = Did the suspect take hostages, threaten to destroy the facility, or use mass violence to force a station decision?
crime-assist-question-wassomeoneattacked = Was someone attacked or held by force?
crime-assist-question-wasitsophont = Was the victim a sapient being?
crime-assist-question-didvictimdie = Did the victim die as a result of the attack?
crime-assist-question-isvictimremovedfrombody = Was the body destroyed, spaced, or hidden until rot so revival is impossible?
crime-assist-question-wasdeathintentional = Did the suspect act with intent to kill?
crime-assist-question-forcedmindbreakertoxin = Was the victim subjected to mind control, brainwashing, or forced psychological harm?
crime-assist-question-hadillicititem = Did the suspect have an illicit item, substance, or piece of restricted gear?
crime-assist-question-wasitaperson = Did the suspect unlawfully confine another sapient being against their will?
crime-assist-question-wassuspectselling = Was the suspect selling or distributing weapons, explosives, or other illicit items?
crime-assist-question-wassuspectseentaking = Can it be proven that the suspect took the item knowing they were not allowed to have it?
crime-assist-question-isitemextremelydangerous = Is the item a firearm, combat blade, grenade, explosive, or anti-corporate equipment?
crime-assist-question-wassuspectinarestrictedlocation = Was the suspect somewhere they had no lawful access to?
crime-assist-question-wasentrancelocked = Was it a secure area (bridge, heads' offices, security, armory, vault, telecoms, EVA, AI core, atmos, engine, or captain's quarters)?
crime-assist-question-didsuspectbreaksomething = Did the suspect damage property?
crime-assist-question-weretheremanysuspects = Were several suspects acting as a group that refused to disperse?
crime-assist-question-wasdamagesmall = Was the damage minor (graffiti, litter, cosmetic mess) and easily undone?
crime-assist-question-wasdestroyeditemimportanttostation = Was a key station system or a large area damaged (power, cloning, atmos, explosives)?
crime-assist-question-islargepartofstationdestroyed = Was the whole facility threatened, or was self-destruct / mass hostage-taking used to force compliance?
crime-assist-question-wascrimesexualinnature = Was it a threat or use of force of a sexual nature?
crime-assist-question-wassuspectanuisance = Was the suspect disrupting public order or refusing lawful orders?
crime-assist-question-falselyreportingtosecurity = Did the suspect make a report to security, in person or over radio, that was proven intentionally false?
crime-assist-question-happenincourt = Did the suspect refuse lawful orders during a hearing or interrogation?
crime-assist-question-duringactiveinvestigation = Did the suspect obstruct a lawful investigation, search, or arrest?
crime-assist-question-tocommandstaff = Did the suspect take part in an armed uprising against lawful corporate authority?
crime-assist-question-wasitcommanditself = Did a head of staff or command grossly neglect their duties, causing death or a station disaster?
crime-assist-crimedetail-innocent = No article applies. Use your judgement. A warning is often enough for a first minor incident in the same _XX category.
crime-assist-crimedetail-animalcruelty = Maliciously inflicting suffering on a non-sapient animal, outside legal medical, research, or pest-control work. Ian is charged at the top of the range.
crime-assist-crimedetail-theft = Taking common or departmental property the suspect has no right to, including gear from a department they do not belong to. Return plus a warning is enough in petty cases. PDA theft is §202. Rare station property is §302. High-value register items are §502.
crime-assist-crimedetail-trespass = Entering an unsecured area without permission (department floors without access, storage, maintenance). A head's ban overrides a worker's invitation. Combine with theft if both apply (_XX differs).
crime-assist-crimedetail-vandalism = Defacing or interfering with property without serious damage (graffiti, unauthorized cosmetic rebuilds, littering). Breaking a window is §204.
crime-assist-crimedetail-hooliganism = Disrupting public order, including taking part in a riot. Public nudity, insults, obstructing officers, and incitement count. The organizer answers for the group. Armed revolt is §500.
crime-assist-crimedetail-manslaughter = Killing a sapient being without intent. Apply the "no intent" circumstance to §401. Each further victim is a separate charge.
crime-assist-crimedetail-grandtheft = Theft of rare or critical station property that is not on the high-value register (non-register boards, mechs, security access keys, departmental remotes, non-register head IDs, hardsuits, jetpacks). Register items are §502.
crime-assist-crimedetail-blackmarketeering = Selling or giving away weapons, weapon parts, ammo, grenades, or explosives, including homemade ones. Possession without trafficking is §303. Anti-corporate register items are §503.
crime-assist-crimedetail-sabotage = Deliberate property damage: broken windows, welded or blocked doors, stripping gear or furniture off someone else's workplace without that department's leave. Sabotage of key systems is §304 or §504.
crime-assist-crimedetail-mindbreaking = Serious psychological harm from confinement, blackmail, or mind control. Death of the victim is §401.
crime-assist-crimedetail-assault = Unlawful threat of force or light force without consent: intimidation, attempted strikes, beating, light injury, stunning, brief tying. Do not stack with §301 on the same victim. Heavy wounds, crit, or unlawful holding are §301.
crime-assist-crimedetail-abuseofpower = Serious neglect by a head of staff, or inaction that kills crew or wrecks the station: deaths from a head's failure to act, refusing aid to someone in crit, or a severe abuse of authority. Demotion is separate from brig time.
crime-assist-crimedetail-possession = Possession of illegal or contraband weapons (unlicensed firearms, combat blades, grenades, explosives, non-register Syndicate weapons, explosive implants). Sale is §403. Anti-corporate register items are §503.
crime-assist-crimedetail-endangerment = Breach of duty that endangers people or the station: workplace accidents from neglect, unauthorized experiments, medical malpractice, or failing to act when harm was likely. A bare refusal of an order, with no danger, is §200.
crime-assist-crimedetail-breakingandentering = Entering without permission: bridge, heads' offices, security, armory, vault, telecoms, EVA, AI core, atmos, engine, or captain's quarters. Does not stack with §105.
crime-assist-crimedetail-rioting = Taking part in a group that disrupts public order and will not disperse. The organizer answers for the group's acts. Armed revolt against lawful corporate authority is §500.
crime-assist-crimedetail-contemptofcourt = Resisting lawful orders from authority or during a legal arrest: refusing a lawful order, warrant, or search; resisting arrest; removing cuffs; helping someone avoid arrest; brig-rule breaches that are not an escape. The order must be lawful. Cell escape is §300.
crime-assist-crimedetail-perjuryfalsereport = Knowingly making a false report to security or lying in a way that obstructs a lawful investigation. Depending on the act this may also be §100 or §206.
crime-assist-crimedetail-obstructionofjustice = Interfering with a lawful investigation, search, or arrest, or helping someone avoid detention. Cell escape is §300.
crime-assist-crimedetail-murder = Intentional or negligent killing of a sapient being, including blocking crit aid until they die, or driving them to suicide. The body must still be revivable. Three or more intentional killings are a standalone ground for permabrig. Destroying the body is §501.
crime-assist-crimedetail-terrorism = Acts that threaten to destroy the ship or facility, or that force decisions through mass violence: starting self-destruct, explosives used for blackmail, hostage-taking, seizing the ship. A formal execution needs an execution warrant.
crime-assist-crimedetail-grandsabotage = Widespread destruction of an area or a key station system (explosives, sabotaging power, cloning, or atmos). Deliberately wrecking the whole facility is §504.
crime-assist-crimedetail-decorporealisation = Bringing a body to a state where revival is impossible: gibbing, spacing, or hiding it until it rots. Killing without destroying the corpse is §401.
crime-assist-crimedetail-kidnapping = Unlawful restriction of liberty, forced movement, or imprisonment of a sapient being. Psychological harm from confinement, blackmail, or mind control also falls here. Death is §401.
crime-assist-crimedetail-sedition = An armed group action that actually threatens lawful corporate authority, whether spontaneous or planned. Armed means firearms, melee weapons, or tools that can quickly cause grievous harm. Unarmed disorder is §100.
crime-assist-crimedetail-sexualharassment = Space Law has no separate sexual article. Charge as §201 assault (threat or light force) or §301 if it caused grievous physical or psychological harm or unlawful confinement.
